From: mayipashu <mayipashu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: mt7915: make the NPU RX path observable

With NPU RX enabled the firmware arms the host rings (base/count are
written to 0x30d180/0x30d190) but never produces a descriptor: producer
and consumer stay 0 and the NPU WLAN interrupt status stays clear, while
mt7915_dma_enable() masks the host MAIN/BAND1 RX interrupts and
mt7915_npu_rx_ring() replaces those host rings. The result is a total
receive stall, so no station can associate.

Two instrumentation gaps made that hard to see:

  - mt7915_npu_debugfs() is never called, because the mt7915 debugfs
    entry point runs before mt7915_npu_init() and therefore always sees
    dev->npu == NULL, so the npu_rx counters entry never exists. Create
    it from debugfs root (this mt76 predates mt76_dev::debugfs_dir).
  - the descriptor base handed to the MT7915 (from
    WLAN_FUNC_GET_WAIT_RXDESC_BASE), the host ring base published to the
    NPU and the value read back from the MT7915 RX ring registers are not
    logged anywhere.

Log those three values so the next run shows whether the MT7915 ring
really points at the NPU descriptor area and whether the ring registers
took the write.

Signed-off-by: mayipashu <mayipashu@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/mt7915/npu.c
+++ b/mt7915/npu.c
@@ -595,6 +595,13 @@
 		q->irq_added = true;
 	}
 
+	/* Expose the npu_rx counters. mt7915's debugfs entry point runs before
+	 * this function, so it always sees dev->npu == NULL and the file never
+	 * appears; create it from debugfs root instead (this mt76 predates
+	 * mt76_dev::debugfs_dir).
+	 */
+	mt7915_npu_debugfs(dev, NULL);
+
 	/* Reinitialization also changes band 0's force-to-CPU policy. */
 	mutex_lock(&mt7915_npu_lock);
 	err = 0;
@@ -676,10 +683,17 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	q->radio_desc = desc;
+	dev_info(dev->mt76.dev,
+		 "NPU RX ring band%u: radio_regs=%#x bar_reg=%#x desc=%#x count=%u\n",
+		 band, regs, lower_32_bits(base + regs), desc, count);
 	mt76_wr(dev, regs, desc);
 	mt76_wr(dev, regs + 4, count);
 	mt76_wr(dev, regs + 8, count - 1);
 	mt76_wr(dev, regs + 0xc, 0);
+	dev_info(dev->mt76.dev,
+		 "NPU RX band%u radio regs: base=%#x count=%u tail=%#x head=%#x\n",
+		 band, mt76_rr(dev, regs), mt76_rr(dev, regs + 4),
+		 mt76_rr(dev, regs + 8), mt76_rr(dev, regs + 0xc));
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -714,6 +728,9 @@
 		regmap_write(priv->npu->regmap, q->regs + 0xc, 0);
 		dma_wmb();
 		regmap_write(priv->npu->regmap, q->regs, lower_32_bits(q->desc_dma));
+		dev_info(dev->mt76.dev,
+			 "NPU RX start band%u: npu_regs=%#x desc_dma=%pad buf_dma=%pad irq=%d\n",
+			 q->band, q->regs, &q->desc_dma, &q->buf_dma, q->irq);
 		priv->published = true;
 		napi_enable(&q->napi);
 		q->napi_enabled = true;
